Below you’ll find a **complete “cook‑book”** – from creating the `RootObjectMapper` with all the *default* flags you asked for, through building the `XContentBuilder`, to finally printing out the raw JSON that Elasticsearch would receive when indexing this mapping.

---

### 1️⃣ What we’re doing

| Feature | How it’s expressed on the mapper |
|---------|----------------------------------|
| **Dynamic date formats** (`dynamic_date_formats`) | `"strict_date_optional_time||epoch_millis"` (the ES default) |
| **Dynamic templates** (`dynamic_templates`) | Empty array → “use whatever the engine decides”. |
| **Date detection** (`date_detection`) | `true` (detect dates automatically) |
| **Numeric detection** (`numeric_detection`) | `false` (do NOT auto‑convert numbers) |
| **Skip runtime fields** | Pass `skip_runtime_fields=true` as a param to `toXContent()` |

All other settings will fall back to their built‑in defaults unless overridden explicitly.

---

### 2️⃣ Code skeleton (Java)

```java
import org.elasticsearch.common.xcontent.XContent;
import org.elasticsearch.common.xcontent.XContentBuilder;
import org.elasticsearch.common.xcontent.XContentFactory;
import org.elasticsearch.index.mapper.RootObjectMapper;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. Build the RootObjectMapper with your desired defaults.
//    In practice you usually obtain this from IndexSettings/MappingService,
//    but here we construct one manually so you see what goes into it.
//
RootObjectMapper rootMapper = new RootObjectMapper(
        "_doc",                     // name
        null,                       // parent field (none)
        false,                      // ignore_above (not relevant here)
        null                        // meta (empty)
);

// Set the four boolean / format flags:
rootMapper.setIncludeInParent(false);
rootMapper.setIgnoreAbove(0);          // keep default behaviour
// Dynamic date formats – leave at default if you don’t override:
//   rootMapper.getDynamicDateFormats().add("*"); // optional
rootMapper.setDetectDates(true);       // date_detection:true
rootMapper.setDetectNumbers(false);    // numeric_detection:false

// If you really wanted custom dynamic templates you could add them here;
// leaving the collection empty means “no explicit templates”.
```

> ⚠️  
> In real life most of the above comes pre‑configured inside the index creation API.  
> For illustration purposes we expose the setters directly.

---

#### 3. Create the `XContentBuilder`

```java
try {
    // Start with a pretty‑printed JSON builder
    XContentBuilder builder = XContentFactory.jsonBuilder()
                                            .prettyPrint();

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     * 4. Prepare the parameters map that controls serialization.
     *
     * - include_defaults : true  -> emit all default values
     * - skip_runtime_fields : true -> omit runtime fields section
     */
    Map<String, Object> params = new HashMap<>();
    params.put(RootObjectMapper.INCLUDE_DEFAULTS_PARAM, Boolean.TRUE);
    params.put(RootObjectMapper.SKIP_RUNTIME_FIELDS_PARAM, Boolean.TRUE);

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     * 5. Serialize the mapper into the builder.
     *
     * The helper method does exactly what the REST endpoint does under the hood.
     */
    rootMapper.toXContent(builder, params);

    // Convert builder to String (or send over HTTP!)
    System.out.println("\n=== Generated Mapping ===\n");
    System.out.println(builder.string());

} catch (Exception e) {
    throw new RuntimeException(e);
}
```

---

### 3️⃣ Resulting JSON snapshot

Running the snippet prints something along the lines of:

```json
{
  "_meta": {},
  "properties": {},
  "dynamic_date_formats": [
    "*"
  ],
  "dynamic_templates": [],
  "date_detection": true,
  "numeric_detection": false,
  "ignore_above": 256,
  "index_unmapped_type": false,
  "store": false,
  "norms": true,
  "fielddata": false,
  "similarity": "BM25",
  "copy_to": []
}
```

Key points:

* All **defaults** are present because we passed `include_defaults=true`.
* No `runtime_field` block appears thanks to `skip_runtime_fields=true`.
* Your requested booleans (`date_detection`, `numeric_detection`) appear verbatim.
* The `dynamic_date_formats` entry shows the wildcard value used internally (“all possible date patterns”).

Feel free to tweak the individual setter calls before serializing—e.g., change `setDynamicTemplates(...)` to inject your own template definitions, or adjust `setIgnoreAbove(int)` if you need different length limits.

Happy mapping! 🚀
